1
00:00:02,670 --> 00:00:05,000
Looks like the seniors are 
gonna win it all this year.

2
00:00:05,420 --> 00:00:07,380
Maybe not, there are some 
freshman teams left.

3
00:00:09,880 --> 00:00:14,080
I hear class 1-3 is pretty tough to beat.
They've got that one kid with the cornrows.

4
00:00:15,830 --> 00:00:20,080
We wouldn't have lost if you'd made
solid passes like that to me during OUR game.

5
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:23,460
There's no doubt, the biggest mistake
you made in that last play...

6
00:00:23,830 --> 00:00:28,250
...was not looking at the basket
the instant you got your hands on the ball.

7
00:00:34,460 --> 00:00:35,460
Crud...

8
00:00:36,330 --> 00:00:44,130
Kagami ni senaka mukete ayumu 
hodo ni toozakaru yume yo

9
00:00:44,290 --> 00:00:48,630
Massugu kimi to mukiaitai

10
00:00:48,960 --> 00:00:55,250
Dekinai jibun e to "never mind"

11
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:03,130
Ahiru no Sora

12
00:01:04,750 --> 00:01:09,130
Nagare sagyou de waketeyuku yume

13
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:12,420
Muki? Fumuki? Iwaba rongai?

14
00:01:12,500 --> 00:01:16,830
Koe mo naku kietetta koe

15
00:01:17,420 --> 00:01:19,830
Tameiki sura denai

16
00:01:20,210 --> 00:01:26,000
Hito no sei ni shitatte owarenai

17
00:01:26,170 --> 00:01:29,960
Me no mae ni kiritatta ima

18
00:01:29,960 --> 00:01:34,000
"Koetai" to kokoro ga sakenderu

19
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:41,540
Dekinai wake o sagasu nara daredemo dekiru sa

20
00:01:41,750 --> 00:01:49,130
Agaki hashitta sono saki 
mada shiranai jibun to deau

21
00:01:49,420 --> 00:01:55,500
Kabe ni kizamikonda rakugaki to "never mind"

22
00:01:55,670 --> 00:01:59,580
Ima asu e to hazume

23
00:02:07,330 --> 00:02:08,540
Good job out there!

24
00:02:09,670 --> 00:02:11,210
Oh, hi, Nanao.

25
00:02:09,750 --> 00:02:13,580
The Last Piece

26
00:02:12,460 --> 00:02:14,830
Hey! You put on your basketball 
shoes! That's unfair!

27
00:02:14,830 --> 00:02:18,130
Uh, well, my next match against Kite's class
is going to be rough.

28
00:02:18,580 --> 00:02:21,080
I know I can't keep up with him
in the school's gym shoes...

29
00:02:23,790 --> 00:02:27,790
In that last game, you didn't even try
for a single three-pointer.

30
00:02:28,500 --> 00:02:29,130
Why is that?

31
00:02:29,420 --> 00:02:31,630
Well, to be honest...

32
00:02:31,830 --> 00:02:35,080
I'm sure that wasn't just by choice.
You can't shoot properly now, right?

33
00:02:37,170 --> 00:02:38,460
Ouch!

34
00:02:37,670 --> 00:02:39,170
Hello, Chiaki.

35
00:02:39,170 --> 00:02:40,000
Sup?

36
00:02:40,130 --> 00:02:41,330
Ow...

37
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:46,250
You've gotten too afraid of 
missing to make any shots.

38
00:02:46,250 --> 00:02:49,040
It's a mental block that newbies 
often have to deal with.

39
00:02:49,380 --> 00:02:52,500
Screwing up during practice is totally different
from doing it during a game.

40
00:02:53,420 --> 00:02:56,790
There are many situations
where a single mistake can cost the whole game.

41
00:02:57,040 --> 00:02:59,080
It's a traumatic experience for anybody.

42
00:02:59,540 --> 00:03:04,000
But it's my lack of experience in actual games
that's the problem. Is that right?

43
00:03:04,250 --> 00:03:06,790
No. My conclusion is that...

44
00:03:07,330 --> 00:03:09,000
...I'm to blame for all of this.

45
00:03:09,290 --> 00:03:10,540
Huh?

46
00:03:10,540 --> 00:03:13,670
This all proves that you're not capable
of being a good point guard.

47
00:03:14,170 --> 00:03:17,060
Directing the team's offense while 
simultaneously trying to score yourself,

48
00:03:17,060 --> 00:03:19,320
is something far easier said than done.

49
00:03:19,460 --> 00:03:22,920
Not to mention, you're a three-point shooter.

50
00:03:23,880 --> 00:03:26,880
What I should have done,
is just let you play to your strengths.

51
00:03:27,330 --> 00:03:32,500
But instead I've pretty much killed your ability
to shoot anymore threes. Sorry, dude.

52
00:03:32,790 --> 00:03:36,000
That was the least convincing 
apology I've ever heard...

53
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:38,670
You really shouldn't think too hard about it.

54
00:03:39,080 --> 00:03:42,040
You should just keep playing
in the same way that you have been.

55
00:03:44,210 --> 00:03:46,290
But if I just stay the way I am...

56
00:03:46,960 --> 00:03:50,540
...doesn't that doom me to fail again
in any similar situation?

57
00:03:51,790 --> 00:03:53,920
I don't wanna let that happen no matter what!

58
00:03:53,920 --> 00:03:55,040
Seriously?

59
00:03:55,040 --> 00:03:56,710
He sounds like a kid having a fit!

60
00:03:57,460 --> 00:04:00,330
It's not just an issue of 
skill, but also personality!

61
00:04:00,330 --> 00:04:03,830
She's right. Dummies like you
just can't handle being the point guard.

62
00:04:05,460 --> 00:04:10,250
Fine then! I'll go out there and play point guard
while also shooting a bunch of threes!

63
00:04:10,460 --> 00:04:13,330
I can handle that! I'll show all of you!

64
00:04:17,330 --> 00:04:21,920
Nice! Looks like the semi-finals are going to be
match between Kite and lil' Sora's classes!

65
00:04:21,920 --> 00:04:23,960
That means we're in for a real show!

66
00:04:25,580 --> 00:04:28,630
I'm guessing everybody else
on these teams are amateurs.

67
00:04:29,580 --> 00:04:32,540
That basically makes this
a one-on-one game between Kite and Sora.

68
00:04:32,880 --> 00:04:34,420
You're so cool, Natsume!

69
00:04:34,420 --> 00:04:35,500
You can do it!

70
00:04:35,500 --> 00:04:37,040
Show them your moves!

71
00:04:37,880 --> 00:04:39,750
Why are there so many girls here?!

72
00:04:39,750 --> 00:04:42,330
None of them were watching 
the softball matches!

73
00:04:42,920 --> 00:04:44,460
I'm gonna play, too!

74
00:04:44,460 --> 00:04:46,790
Everybody knows you're not a freshman!

75
00:04:46,790 --> 00:04:48,420
I am, I just turned back time.

76
00:04:50,040 --> 00:04:51,080
Hey, shrimp.

77
00:04:51,750 --> 00:04:53,380
Tell me something...

78
00:04:54,040 --> 00:04:55,330
At the end of the Kitasumi match...

79
00:04:55,920 --> 00:04:57,750
...why didn't you pass me the ball?

80
00:04:58,380 --> 00:04:59,790
That's because...

81
00:05:01,210 --> 00:05:03,960
...our team didn't have any stamina left,

82
00:05:03,960 --> 00:05:06,200
so I thought we would lose 
if it went into overtime.

83
00:05:06,460 --> 00:05:08,960
The only one who didn't have 
any stamina left was you.

84
00:05:09,380 --> 00:05:11,500
Who gave you the right to 
throw away our last chance?

85
00:05:11,710 --> 00:05:13,380
I could have kept playing!

86
00:05:15,830 --> 00:05:17,830
Sweet, it's our ball! Pass it here!

87
00:05:24,500 --> 00:05:25,500
He's gonna blow right past him.

88
00:05:26,130 --> 00:05:27,330
Like he always does.

89
00:05:27,790 --> 00:05:29,380
I'm NOT letting him get by me!

90
00:05:29,790 --> 00:05:30,880
Dumbass.

91
00:05:47,500 --> 00:05:48,830
Let's take it nice and slow, guys!

92
00:05:49,080 --> 00:05:49,830
Right!

93
00:05:54,130 --> 00:05:55,330
He's all over me.

94
00:05:56,960 --> 00:05:57,880
Here, Kida!

95
00:05:59,080 --> 00:06:00,540
He's not playing offensively.

96
00:06:01,080 --> 00:06:05,170
I know he's outside of shooting range,
but this is far from his usual play style...

97
00:06:05,630 --> 00:06:07,130
Move in! Head for the basket!

98
00:06:10,710 --> 00:06:12,170
Dammit! It missed!

99
00:06:13,710 --> 00:06:15,250
Whoa! What a lucky grab!

100
00:06:15,460 --> 00:06:16,710
The basket is straight ahead!

101
00:06:16,710 --> 00:06:18,170
I can sink one!
Time for a three!

102
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:21,460
But Tobita is open in low-post!

103
00:06:23,130 --> 00:06:24,130
Too slow.

104
00:06:24,460 --> 00:06:25,580
That idiot.

105
00:06:26,080 --> 00:06:27,540
Guess he's no match for Kite.

106
00:06:33,420 --> 00:06:35,080
Wow, 4 points in the blink of an eye.

107
00:06:35,080 --> 00:06:36,330
They're way too good!

108
00:06:36,670 --> 00:06:38,670
Class 1-3 is winning for sure.

109
00:06:38,880 --> 00:06:40,750
Natsume is just way too cool!

110
00:06:41,960 --> 00:06:45,250
I can't remember, have I always
been this bad at point guard?

111
00:06:46,710 --> 00:06:47,920
I think even mom told me...

112
00:06:48,830 --> 00:06:52,960
Listen, you're an attacker,
which makes you a bad fit for point guard.

113
00:06:56,920 --> 00:06:59,330
I'd really... like to shoot a three.

114
00:07:03,210 --> 00:07:04,040
It's a three!

115
00:07:05,830 --> 00:07:08,040
Stupid fool! You haven't even 
shaken off your defender!

116
00:07:08,380 --> 00:07:11,580
You should just keep playing
in the same way that you have been.

117
00:07:14,580 --> 00:07:15,250
That was slick.

118
00:07:16,250 --> 00:07:17,380
He passed it!

119
00:07:19,250 --> 00:07:21,920
Just playing the same way... 
isn't an option for me!

120
00:07:23,130 --> 00:07:24,330
Shoot it again!

121
00:07:24,330 --> 00:07:25,540
Over here! Pass it back!

122
00:07:25,830 --> 00:07:27,080
Let's back off and regroup!

123
00:07:27,420 --> 00:07:28,960
That was a real surprise.

124
00:07:29,170 --> 00:07:31,080
I never thought he'd go for a pass there.

125
00:07:32,290 --> 00:07:33,920
Let's take our time and not rush!

126
00:07:33,920 --> 00:07:36,630
I wanna win! I'm sick 
of losing over and over!

127
00:07:36,960 --> 00:07:38,960
Kurumatani, over here! Pass it to me!

128
00:07:39,290 --> 00:07:42,630
This damn shrimp...
is he actually going to shoot a three now?

129
00:07:43,630 --> 00:07:44,790
He got distracted!

130
00:07:52,460 --> 00:07:53,170
Dammit!

131
00:07:53,380 --> 00:07:54,630
He's off his game.

132
00:07:55,170 --> 00:07:57,290
Both his timing and his form are sloppy.

133
00:07:57,290 --> 00:07:59,130
Nah, he's got the right idea.

134
00:07:59,130 --> 00:07:59,710
Huh?

135
00:07:59,920 --> 00:08:02,500
Whether he's playing point 
guard or some other position,

136
00:08:02,500 --> 00:08:04,960
it doesn't change the fact 
he needs to focus on scoring.

137
00:08:05,380 --> 00:08:06,790
I'm curious, Chiaki.

138
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:09,880
Do you really believe that 
Kurumatani has no potential...

139
00:08:10,290 --> 00:08:12,330
...in becoming a good point guard?

140
00:08:12,830 --> 00:08:15,000
At the end of the day, he's just a baby bird.

141
00:08:16,500 --> 00:08:19,710
The moment he learns how to really fly...
is still in the future.

142
00:08:21,670 --> 00:08:24,330
Don't worry about dribbling,
let's move the ball with passes!

143
00:08:24,330 --> 00:08:25,330
Right!

144
00:08:26,290 --> 00:08:30,580
A point guard who doubles as a shooter
isn't actually all that hard to find.

145
00:08:30,920 --> 00:08:35,250
But guys who go straight for a three
from the front without a second thought

146
00:08:35,250 --> 00:08:37,670
are just brainless fools 
with no sense for the game.

147
00:08:38,040 --> 00:08:39,500
This shrimp is no different.

148
00:08:40,880 --> 00:08:45,790
I know better than to panic
when a totally ordinary player shoots an open three.

149
00:08:46,630 --> 00:08:50,750
The fact remains that overall accuracy
of three-pointers is relatively low.

150
00:08:54,080 --> 00:08:55,630
But he's another story...

151
00:08:59,710 --> 00:09:00,750
Whoa!

152
00:09:00,750 --> 00:09:01,920
He scored from so far away!

153
00:09:02,250 --> 00:09:05,290
You can tell Natsume has started to hesitate
while playing defense.

154
00:09:05,630 --> 00:09:07,000
That's only natural.

155
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:11,500
Passes are usually the biggest thing
you have to worry about when defending a point guard.

156
00:09:11,830 --> 00:09:16,380
And pulling up tight to prevent shots
only increases the risk of getting shaken off by a drive.

157
00:09:16,880 --> 00:09:20,040
The squirt's height actually works in his favor
in times like these.

158
00:09:20,460 --> 00:09:21,960
Quit standing around like an idiot!

159
00:09:21,960 --> 00:09:23,540
Hurry and pass the ball in!

160
00:09:23,540 --> 00:09:24,710
Uh, right.

161
00:09:24,920 --> 00:09:27,580
That stupid twerp! I'll 
show him how to really-

162
00:09:28,920 --> 00:09:31,380
Game over!

163
00:09:31,630 --> 00:09:34,420
All right! Yahoo!

164
00:09:34,420 --> 00:09:36,330
The winner is class 1-3!

165
00:09:36,330 --> 00:09:38,500
What?! But why?!

166
00:09:38,500 --> 00:09:42,710
The answer to that should be obvious.
It's because you boys didn't score enough points.

167
00:09:42,710 --> 00:09:45,830
Why the hell are you celebrating
over a single three pointer?

168
00:09:45,830 --> 00:09:48,250
You know that's hardly enough 
to beat me, little monkey.

169
00:09:48,250 --> 00:09:50,380
I lost again...

170
00:09:52,790 --> 00:09:55,830
You've got it wrong,
passing and shooting aren't important.

171
00:09:55,830 --> 00:09:56,960
Scoring points is.

172
00:09:58,630 --> 00:10:01,750
You couldn't score enough points by the end,
and that's why you lost.

173
00:10:01,750 --> 00:10:02,580
Fool.

174
00:10:04,330 --> 00:10:07,580
The real problem is that 6 minutes
aren't enough to play a decent game!

175
00:10:10,080 --> 00:10:11,380
Tell me something, Nanao.

176
00:10:11,580 --> 00:10:12,420
Yes?

177
00:10:12,420 --> 00:10:14,960
If you're planning on making 
Sora our point guard,

178
00:10:14,960 --> 00:10:17,170
does that mean you want Chiaki
to switch to shooting guard?

179
00:10:17,170 --> 00:10:19,670
That's definitely one possible arrangement.

180
00:10:19,670 --> 00:10:21,790
In terms of enhancing our 
offensive capabilities,

181
00:10:21,790 --> 00:10:26,170
it's absolutely fundamental for Kurumatani
to be the one who serves as the point guard.

182
00:10:26,880 --> 00:10:31,420
If we find a way to make my ideal plan a reality,
then Kuzu High will become even stronger.

183
00:10:31,880 --> 00:10:34,710
I gotta admit, this little 
lady is really something else.

184
00:10:35,580 --> 00:10:38,040
We don't have a lot of time 
until the prelims start up.

185
00:10:38,420 --> 00:10:39,960
We'll just have to do what we can.

186
00:10:40,830 --> 00:10:43,880
But to put us in the most 
ideal position possible,

187
00:10:43,880 --> 00:10:46,210
we're going to need one more 
player to join the team.

188
00:10:46,210 --> 00:10:46,830
Huh?

189
00:10:47,210 --> 00:10:50,880
Of course, the fact remains that we only have
7 players on the team right now.

190
00:10:50,880 --> 00:10:52,830
So I'm trying to keep my 
expectations realistic.

191
00:10:53,960 --> 00:10:57,880
Okay, so, give me an example.
What kind of guy are we talking about?

192
00:10:57,880 --> 00:10:59,250
Do we need another forward?

193
00:10:59,710 --> 00:11:01,330
Well, I think...

194
00:11:09,830 --> 00:11:12,330
Holy shit, that dude's a giant!

195
00:11:12,330 --> 00:11:14,130
The sloping shoulders champ, for sure.

196
00:11:14,130 --> 00:11:16,420
I'm pretty sure that guy has
at least 5 centimeters on you, Chiaki!

197
00:11:16,420 --> 00:11:19,460
Nah, I'd win if I squished my 
afro to give it more height.

198
00:11:24,380 --> 00:11:26,170
Time for the semi-finals of B block!

199
00:11:26,170 --> 00:11:29,210
Students from class 1-7 and 3-6, line up!

200
00:11:29,630 --> 00:11:31,330
That kid is like skyscraper.

201
00:11:31,330 --> 00:11:32,420
And so thin...

202
00:11:32,420 --> 00:11:35,630
Whoa! What the hell? What kind of bean
did that stalk sprout from?!

203
00:11:35,960 --> 00:11:37,920
Think he's got any experience shooting hoops?

204
00:11:37,920 --> 00:11:39,710
Or maybe he was on a volleyball team?

205
00:11:39,710 --> 00:11:43,080
His class managed to survive up to the semi-finals,
so he's gotta have some skills.

206
00:11:43,380 --> 00:11:45,040
S-so huge!

207
00:11:45,380 --> 00:11:48,460
Who is that?! How tall is 
he?! What's he been eating?!

208
00:11:48,750 --> 00:11:52,000
He's a freshman from class 7, uh,
I think they called him Mokichi?

209
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:54,460
Mokichi! He sounds like a samurai!

210
00:11:54,710 --> 00:11:57,210
I bet he's nothing more than a giant oaf.

211
00:11:57,460 --> 00:11:59,540
We're counting on you, Mokichi!

212
00:11:59,540 --> 00:12:02,000
You're gonna be our wall that 
defends the basket, okay?

213
00:12:10,920 --> 00:12:12,290
He fell down again!

214
00:12:12,290 --> 00:12:13,790
I hear he's anemic or something.

215
00:12:13,790 --> 00:12:15,880
That's like the fifth time 
he's hit the floor today.

216
00:12:17,210 --> 00:12:18,380
The hell was that?

217
00:12:18,380 --> 00:12:20,420
What did he even get on the court for?

218
00:12:20,420 --> 00:12:22,580
I bet he'd make a good lackey.

219
00:12:23,540 --> 00:12:27,500
For just a second, I envisioned 
having the perfect team...

220
00:12:28,290 --> 00:12:29,040
Scram!

221
00:12:29,040 --> 00:12:30,040
Get out the way!

222
00:12:30,040 --> 00:12:31,080
Prepare to get wasted!

223
00:12:31,290 --> 00:12:34,710
Oh jeez, this is hopeless.
You gotta go defend the basket!

224
00:12:34,710 --> 00:12:37,290
Don't be stupid, the 
seniors are way too scary!

225
00:12:37,290 --> 00:12:39,880
Man, and we made it all the 
way to the semi-finals...

226
00:12:41,210 --> 00:12:43,460
Hey, hurry and pass the ball in!

227
00:12:45,330 --> 00:12:46,960
Oh, he woke up.

228
00:12:50,250 --> 00:12:52,000
Is the match over?

229
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:55,330
Far from it! We actually just 
got started a minute ago!

230
00:12:55,330 --> 00:12:57,750
Hurry up and sub in! All you 
gotta do is stand around!

231
00:12:59,830 --> 00:13:01,040
Player substitution!

232
00:13:04,960 --> 00:13:06,250
That dude is so huge!

233
00:13:06,250 --> 00:13:08,290
His reach is unbelievable.

234
00:13:08,290 --> 00:13:11,460
With height like that, even guarding
in high-post must be a piece of cake.

235
00:13:11,790 --> 00:13:13,920
How the hell are you so tall?!

236
00:13:15,790 --> 00:13:18,080
24 second violation! Senior's ball!

237
00:13:19,920 --> 00:13:21,210
C'mon, man...

238
00:13:23,880 --> 00:13:26,460
He's saying that you only 
told him to "stand around."

239
00:13:26,460 --> 00:13:28,170
Just speak normally!

240
00:13:28,380 --> 00:13:32,210
How awesome! I wonder if he would consider
joining the basketball team?

241
00:13:32,210 --> 00:13:35,540
Dumbass! Adding someone like him
to the team is pointless.

242
00:13:35,960 --> 00:13:38,130
What good is having another 
rank amateur going to do?

243
00:13:38,630 --> 00:13:42,040
But having height like his 
is a weapon of its own.

244
00:13:42,710 --> 00:13:45,210
I despise teams that play 
by relying on height.

245
00:13:45,670 --> 00:13:48,080
Because I believe in using 
speed and technique to win.

246
00:13:49,330 --> 00:13:52,330
I thought that made us 
two birds of a feather,

247
00:13:52,500 --> 00:13:54,210
but I guess I had you pegged wrong.

248
00:13:56,380 --> 00:14:01,000
He's not wrong, that's exactly
how I forged my path in basketball.

249
00:14:01,630 --> 00:14:04,750
But the important thing isn't 
how I play as an individual,

250
00:14:04,750 --> 00:14:07,150
but how we play together as a team.

251
00:14:08,380 --> 00:14:10,670
C'mon, freak! Hand over the damn ball!

252
00:14:11,170 --> 00:14:14,330
The bigger they are, the harder they fall
when you push 'em!

253
00:14:18,960 --> 00:14:19,630
Huh?

254
00:14:21,460 --> 00:14:22,670
A hook shot!

255
00:14:27,210 --> 00:14:28,420
What was that?!

256
00:14:28,420 --> 00:14:31,130
He just chucked it and 
somehow scored a basket...

257
00:14:38,670 --> 00:14:42,670
I've never seen anyone make a hook shot
as clean as that one before!

258
00:14:43,790 --> 00:14:45,920
So, his name's "Mokichi"?

259
00:14:46,460 --> 00:14:50,040
The dude just made a lucky shot,
even I can do that sometimes.

260
00:14:50,040 --> 00:14:51,960
You've never even come close, dude.

261
00:14:52,540 --> 00:14:54,130
That's what we call a hook shot.

262
00:14:54,130 --> 00:14:54,750
Huh?

263
00:14:54,960 --> 00:14:57,020
Unlike the standard basketball shot,

264
00:14:57,020 --> 00:15:00,330
you shoot it with your body turned 
perpendicular to the basket.

265
00:14:57,960 --> 00:15:02,080
Standard

266
00:15:00,710 --> 00:15:03,170
It puts the ball father from the defender,

267
00:15:02,080 --> 00:15:07,000
Hook

268
00:15:03,170 --> 00:15:06,360
so it's hard for them to block 
even with a height advantage.

269
00:15:07,250 --> 00:15:11,460
Oh yeah? So if a tall guy like him shoots it,
then it's basically unstoppable.

270
00:15:11,460 --> 00:15:12,500
That's right!

271
00:15:12,830 --> 00:15:15,670
They shoved him off balance
before he even tried to shoot,

272
00:15:15,670 --> 00:15:19,420
but it still sailed right into the hoop,
which means he's damn good.

273
00:15:19,420 --> 00:15:21,040
I have my doubts about that.

274
00:15:21,710 --> 00:15:27,420
It's not exactly rare for any type of shot,
hook shots included, to go in just by chance.

275
00:15:27,750 --> 00:15:31,380
Chucky could be right, it 
might have been pure luck.

276
00:15:31,580 --> 00:15:32,920
That's true.

277
00:15:32,920 --> 00:15:36,290
A single hook shot is only halfway towards
proving his potential skill.

278
00:15:36,750 --> 00:15:38,790
"Halfway"? Whaddya mean?

279
00:15:40,500 --> 00:15:41,380
Well...

280
00:15:41,380 --> 00:15:43,380
Mokichi! Score another one!

281
00:15:43,380 --> 00:15:45,080
Stupid lanky bastard!

282
00:15:45,080 --> 00:15:47,380
I'm not gonna let you pull 
that weird move again!

283
00:15:47,750 --> 00:15:49,460
His defender came at the ball this time.

284
00:15:49,670 --> 00:15:51,290
He can't shoot a hook like that.

285
00:16:02,880 --> 00:16:03,790
Amazing...

286
00:16:03,790 --> 00:16:06,460
His arm was raised even higher 
than the rim on that shot!

287
00:16:06,710 --> 00:16:09,540
Whoa, he shot it with 
his left hand this time!

288
00:16:09,540 --> 00:16:11,920
So he's ambidextrous? That's badass!

289
00:16:12,330 --> 00:16:14,130
He's not ambidextrous.

290
00:16:14,130 --> 00:16:16,920
Any good hook shooter trains 
to do it with both hands.

291
00:16:17,710 --> 00:16:20,960
There's no point to the move
if they can't shoot from either side.

292
00:16:21,790 --> 00:16:24,250
But now, we know it wasn't just a fluke.

293
00:16:24,250 --> 00:16:25,130
Yep.

294
00:16:26,380 --> 00:16:28,380
He's the real deal.

295
00:16:31,380 --> 00:16:34,170
Good to know the finals won't 
be a complete bore for me.

296
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:38,290
At 8 points to 6, the winner is class 1-7!

297
00:16:39,170 --> 00:16:41,080
Sweet! We made it to the finals!

298
00:16:41,920 --> 00:16:43,500
Nice, Mokichi!

299
00:16:43,500 --> 00:16:44,670
Keep it up, dude!

300
00:16:44,960 --> 00:16:48,630
C'mon! C'mon! C'mon! Down here!
Down here! High-five! High-five!

301
00:16:48,630 --> 00:16:50,040
Yay!

302
00:16:50,630 --> 00:16:53,250
Awesome! You're so cool! Nice moves!

303
00:16:54,880 --> 00:16:56,130
Thanks...

304
00:16:56,630 --> 00:16:58,420
Wait. Who are you?

305
00:16:58,420 --> 00:17:01,790
I'm Sora Kurumatani from class 1-4!
Nice to meet you guys!

306
00:17:03,960 --> 00:17:06,670
So hey, Mokichi. Did you 
used to play basketball?

307
00:17:06,880 --> 00:17:07,670
A little.

308
00:17:07,670 --> 00:17:08,710
I knew it!

309
00:17:09,420 --> 00:17:11,250
Mind if I ask how tall you are?

310
00:17:11,250 --> 00:17:12,960
198 centimeters...

311
00:17:12,960 --> 00:17:14,960
A-are you kidding me?!

312
00:17:14,960 --> 00:17:17,380
I'm barely 165 centimeters myself!

313
00:17:18,380 --> 00:17:22,500
Sorry, that was a bit of a 
lie. I'm actually just 160...

314
00:17:22,630 --> 00:17:23,670
Actually 149 centimeters tall

315
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:28,630
It must be hard... to play
on the basketball team at your height.

316
00:17:28,880 --> 00:17:31,460
Uh, well, it can be.

317
00:17:31,460 --> 00:17:34,420
But it's no problem! I don't 
consider it a handicap at all!

318
00:17:34,420 --> 00:17:36,580
I can play just fine, shortness be damned!

319
00:17:37,630 --> 00:17:38,830
That's impressive.

320
00:17:40,630 --> 00:17:43,130
Although, to be perfectly honest...

321
00:17:43,130 --> 00:17:47,040
there are times I kinda wish I had 
grown at least 10 more centimeters.

322
00:17:49,460 --> 00:17:53,250
When I see tall people like you,
I can't help but feel jealous.

323
00:17:57,790 --> 00:18:00,500
Well, I am... jealous of you.

324
00:18:00,790 --> 00:18:01,710
Huh?

325
00:18:10,250 --> 00:18:12,330
WHAAAAAT?!

326
00:18:12,420 --> 00:18:14,250
While his technique seems solid,
Crap! Mokichi went down again!

327
00:18:14,250 --> 00:18:16,040
Agh! We're about to play in the finals!

328
00:18:14,250 --> 00:18:17,040
I'm not really sure he'd 
be very useful to our team.

329
00:18:16,040 --> 00:18:18,080
Yo! Somebody get a stretcher! Hurry!

330
00:18:17,040 --> 00:18:18,080
Yeah.

331
00:18:21,380 --> 00:18:26,880
Class 1 - 7

332
00:18:21,830 --> 00:18:23,130
Oh, Mokichi?

333
00:18:23,130 --> 00:18:26,630
Yeah. I wanted to make sure he recovered
after that nasty fall.

334
00:18:27,130 --> 00:18:30,580
He's fine, don't worry. He 
falls like that all the time.

335
00:18:30,580 --> 00:18:32,500
It's why he's always staying home sick.

336
00:18:32,750 --> 00:18:35,210
That explains why I've never 
seen him around before.

337
00:18:35,210 --> 00:18:38,040
If you want to talk to him,
you should check the chemistry lab.

338
00:18:39,500 --> 00:18:43,500
Team practice should be starting about now,
so I need to make this quick.

339
00:18:43,790 --> 00:18:44,500
Chemistry Club

340
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:46,750
YEOWCH!

341
00:18:47,830 --> 00:18:49,170
Ow, ow, ow...

342
00:18:49,460 --> 00:18:51,210
Watch where you're... ah!

343
00:18:51,210 --> 00:18:52,380
Mokichi!

344
00:18:52,880 --> 00:18:54,000
Are you okay?!

345
00:18:55,130 --> 00:18:57,130
Yeah. I'm all right.

346
00:18:57,880 --> 00:18:59,500
You don't look all right!

347
00:18:59,500 --> 00:19:01,710
It's dissolving! Your coat is dissolving!

348
00:19:01,750 --> 00:19:04,710
Chemistry Lab

349
00:19:02,670 --> 00:19:04,670
He was carrying sulfuric acid...?

350
00:19:04,920 --> 00:19:07,500
Holy crap, I nearly got soaked in that stuff!

351
00:19:10,580 --> 00:19:11,880
What can I do for you?

352
00:19:12,540 --> 00:19:15,080
Uh, nothing, I just...

353
00:19:15,080 --> 00:19:17,330
...was curious what the chemistry club does.

354
00:19:17,920 --> 00:19:19,330
We do experiments and stuff.

355
00:19:20,420 --> 00:19:21,830
And you enjoy doing that?

356
00:19:22,670 --> 00:19:23,670
Yeah.

357
00:19:26,500 --> 00:19:29,000
Pencil lead is made from a solid carbon.

358
00:19:29,420 --> 00:19:32,750
It conducts electricity, so a charge sent through
will make it heat up and glow.

359
00:19:32,750 --> 00:19:33,710
Oh yeah?

360
00:19:34,330 --> 00:19:38,420
Hey Kurumatani! Basketball practice
started a while ago, you're late!

361
00:19:39,790 --> 00:19:41,880
Sorry, I got absorbed and 
lost track of time...

362
00:19:41,880 --> 00:19:44,540
Jeez! We need to practice as much as we can
before the prelims start!

363
00:19:44,540 --> 00:19:47,920
Uh, I'm so sorry for butting 
in on your club everyone!

364
00:19:52,290 --> 00:19:54,500
Your name was... Mokichi, right?

365
00:19:54,830 --> 00:19:57,040
Do you have any interest in 
joining the basketball team?

366
00:19:57,380 --> 00:19:59,790
I'm already in the chemistry club.

367
00:19:59,790 --> 00:20:02,460
Yeah, that much was obvious to me.

368
00:20:02,960 --> 00:20:05,670
It's totally fine with me
if you split your time between both.

369
00:20:05,670 --> 00:20:10,130
I just don't want you to miss the opportunity,
since you seem like you can play well.

370
00:20:10,420 --> 00:20:13,880
Of course, it all comes down
to how you feel about it personally.

371
00:20:14,290 --> 00:20:17,920
But I know a hook shot isn't a skill
that players learn very easily,

372
00:20:17,920 --> 00:20:21,630
so I figure you probably have some experience
playing back in middle school.

373
00:20:22,170 --> 00:20:25,290
I'm just guessing, but I think you must share our
passion for the game.

374
00:20:29,460 --> 00:20:33,580
The truth is... I don't have
much physical strength or stamina.

375
00:20:34,330 --> 00:20:37,920
I wanted to find at least one skill
that I could use to my advantage.

376
00:20:39,130 --> 00:20:44,170
So, I just focused on practicing hook shots
ever since I was in grade school.

377
00:20:46,420 --> 00:20:48,800
Well, you don't have to give 
me an answer right now.

378
00:20:48,800 --> 00:20:51,380
Please just take some time to consider it.

379
00:20:51,750 --> 00:20:53,080
Okay then.

380
00:20:54,250 --> 00:20:56,420
See you later, Mokichi! Bye-bye!

381
00:20:57,040 --> 00:20:58,500
My name isn't Mokichi.

382
00:21:00,460 --> 00:21:03,960
It's Shigeyoshi. Kaname Shigeyoshi.

383
00:21:05,790 --> 00:21:08,170
I think he has a ton of potential, you guys!

384
00:21:08,170 --> 00:21:10,880
We should do whatever we can to get him
to join the basketball team!

385
00:21:11,290 --> 00:21:15,500
I'm against that idea.
He seemed like a big waste of space to me.

386
00:21:15,710 --> 00:21:18,000
Having him would cut our 
chances of playing, too.

387
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:18,920
Totally.

388
00:21:19,080 --> 00:21:21,250
Oh please, don't give me that!

389
00:21:21,250 --> 00:21:24,170
This is the perfect chance to boost
our player pool and bench strength!

390
00:21:24,710 --> 00:21:26,130
Don't you think so, Kurumatani?

391
00:21:29,830 --> 00:21:33,040
So, I just focused on 
practicing hook shots...

392
00:21:35,290 --> 00:21:37,040
The three-pointer?

393
00:21:37,040 --> 00:21:38,040
That's right.

394
00:21:38,420 --> 00:21:40,710
Master that, and then even you can fly!

395
00:21:41,250 --> 00:21:44,630
I honestly don't care if he 
makes us stronger or better,

396
00:21:45,330 --> 00:21:48,920
I just really want to play 
some basketball with Mokichi!

397
00:22:12,880 --> 00:22:17,790
Hitori ja umaku ikanaku temo

398
00:22:18,330 --> 00:22:22,000
Kikkake nante tanjun sa

399
00:22:23,920 --> 00:22:28,960
Mienai deguchi ni hikaru ga sashite

400
00:22:29,420 --> 00:22:33,130
Asu wa soko ni arunda

401
00:22:33,750 --> 00:22:39,830
Hitori nanka ja nakatta

402
00:22:39,830 --> 00:22:45,040
Kono me ni utsuru keshiki no naka ni

403
00:22:45,040 --> 00:22:51,380
Kimi ga ireba doko made datte ikeru sa

404
00:22:51,380 --> 00:22:56,250
Kitto genkai nante nainda

405
00:22:56,250 --> 00:23:01,420
Kimi to ireba tsuyoku narunda

406
00:23:01,630 --> 00:23:08,500
Nando demo tachiagatte susunde ikou

407
00:23:08,630 --> 00:23:16,540
Oh oh oh, oh oh oh, oh oh oh,

408
00:23:16,540 --> 00:23:19,500
Saigo no ichibyou made

409
00:23:19,710 --> 00:23:22,330
Akiramenaide busukatte

410
00:23:22,330 --> 00:23:29,420
Kono michi no saki wa 
kanarazu kagayaiteru kara

411
00:23:30,960 --> 00:23:35,420
Ahiru no Sora
Next Time: The Moon and the Hoop

412
00:23:31,710 --> 00:23:34,250
Next time: "The Moon and the Hoop."

